                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0f9d61c5-b900-4141-b08e-bf8a98a39385",
                        "entry_id": "77cde210-59f9-384a-9e79-8e009067e8c5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "fragmentables"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f480cc13-a871-3139-8795-50d6e325c51c",
                        "entry_id": "77cde210-59f9-384a-9e79-8e009067e8c5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui peut être fragmenté."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7961844-afa9-4f89-9c1f-56e6809739e2",
                                "sense_id": "f480cc13-a871-3139-8795-50d6e325c51c",
                                "text": "Si le support n’est pas transportable ni fragmentable, le prélèvement des taches suspectes sera fait sur place."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e08cd6d-4ee1-494c-a27e-5a223698ead8",
                                "sense_id": "f480cc13-a871-3139-8795-50d6e325c51c",
                                "text": "Plus le travail est fragmentable, plus il perdra de son \" caractère féminin \" : s’il faut encore, aux yeux de certains, être une femme pour avoir \"l’instinct maternel\", moins nombreux sont ceux qui arrivent à justifier d’arbitraires \"talents féminins\" quand il s’agit de faire fonctionner un lave-vaisselle ou d’éplucher des pommes de terre."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9b8caad2-6d46-332c-af1f-2a520d49e3e4",
                        "entry_id": "77cde210-59f9-384a-9e79-8e009067e8c5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui peut au fil du temps se décomposer en nombreux fragments."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "42cf36cb-3d46-47e8-af30-a0abcacbf5f8",
                                "sense_id": "9b8caad2-6d46-332c-af1f-2a520d49e3e4",
                                "text": "Reste surtout à définir correctement ses bioplastiques afin d’éviter des abus de langage à l’image de ce qui a pu se passer en 2005 pour le néosac, annoncé par ses fabricants comme biodégradable alors qu’il n’était que fragmentable sous l’action de la lumière."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "605b79cc-7c7c-498f-b04a-8b45618b3d48",
                                "sense_id": "9b8caad2-6d46-332c-af1f-2a520d49e3e4",
                                "text": "Si de loin le décor est idyllique, entre les grains de sable c’est une autre histoire. Celle des microplastiques polluant le littoral de leurs milliers de fragments. Non le plastique n’est pas biodégradable, mais il est bel et bien fragmentable."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "47d8ccef-1994-4a35-9d82-19996e98fbae",
                        "source_entry_id": "77cde210-59f9-384a-9e79-8e009067e8c5",
                        "target_lang_word": "breakable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "breakable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9cb3317a-2eb3-37f7-90e1-a22442285f74",
                                        "entry_id": "d945fd70-bc48-3edd-925f-5fbbdca84d89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Able to break or be broken."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "426f0859-b279-4fe0-9130-ab4beec8853b",
                                                "sense_id": "9cb3317a-2eb3-37f7-90e1-a22442285f74",
                                                "text": "The accident was also one of several since Clapham […] that demonstrated the role of breakable windows in the death toll. RSSB research would later confirm and reinforce the need for laminated glass to protect passengers and increase survivability."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b4b79f1-821b-3966-84e5-cdfaf21b97d9",
                                        "entry_id": "d945fd70-bc48-3edd-925f-5fbbdca84d89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fragile."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a770472-1350-47ba-bde2-2c66fc20245b",
                                                "sense_id": "9b4b79f1-821b-3966-84e5-cdfaf21b97d9",
                                                "text": "Next Christmas she sent us bisque dolls, very lovely but too breakable to hug; we could not even kiss them but they cracked."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "breakable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30d131f6-3153-3e57-8054-b7215d91b520",
                                        "entry_id": "762959b5-a15a-3e29-9e17-f6b4c1deeeb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that is (easily) breakable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09921826-8f99-4258-8b4b-dc5f9a3d5897",
                                                "sense_id": "30d131f6-3153-3e57-8054-b7215d91b520",
                                                "text": "We had to wrap all the breakables before the movers arrived."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "653cb803-e720-4922-835d-ca6b65d7ed6e",
                                                "sense_id": "30d131f6-3153-3e57-8054-b7215d91b520",
                                                "text": "She was, she wrote, “impatient and absent-minded, prone to drop things intentionally or through clumsiness, even breakables like dishes and love affairs; a woman who is perennially on the move, changing jobs and homes at the drop of a hat and inventing reasons afterward while she is packing; a person who runs away as soon as she gets nervous, long before she smells danger.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "44f2863d-b6a1-3aaf-926f-505529412b12",
                                        "entry_id": "762959b5-a15a-3e29-9e17-f6b4c1deeeb9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A set of customized hardware that is part of a drum kit. Breakables typically consist of: the drummer's cymbals including high-hats, the snare drum, the kick pedal and the drummer's stool."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural-normally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
